#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151973 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "327d9a77-b2dd-57b1-b959-570684714bf9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Trendline of a Given Scatter Plot"}] :question/id #uuid "dd9a05fb-f01c-5ec2-a984-9d73584065ef" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-9683" :question/problem "Which of the lines $p,q,r$, or $s$ is the trend line of the scatter plot above?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2609/Source/Images/65c7bafdfde0ba8015d87c0888f1bdcd.png)" :question/worked-solution "The plot shows that the data points are scattered along a curve, not a straight line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2609/Source/Images/0e32e7767c5353f75f4d693d454192a4.png)\n\nTherefore, there is no linear trend in the data."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151974 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/id #uuid "245065cc-c95c-5f93-bf7d-bbb6412a27e9" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-9694" :question/problem "Determine the equation of the trend line shown above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2609/Source/Images/9bb0151238440704095e29f3bd632b5f.png)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points\n\n$$\n(x_1,y_1)=(-4,5)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(x_2,y_2)=(5,-4)\n$$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form\n\n$$\ny=mx+b\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= (-4 - 5)/(5 - (-4)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{-9}{9} \\\\\n&=-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-1$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny =-x + b\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b$. We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(5,-4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= -x + b \\\\\n- 4 &= -5 + b \\\\\n1 &= b \\\\\nb &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is\n\n$$\ny =-x + 1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151975 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "890526df-fd1a-5340-8732-efc0c1a1b0ae" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/id #uuid "1a299957-af22-544b-af37-695f45065a3e" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-9695" :question/problem "Estimate the equation of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round both the slope and the $y$-intercept to the nearest $0.5$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2609/Source/Images/ebdab620e3e2f624fd9b67cec07fee36.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2609/Source/Images/f09eeb54cefd8a6e6c7de8a1508acae8.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through\n\n$$\n(x_1,y_1)\\approx(4,4)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(x_2,y_2)\\approx(6,7)\n$$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form\n\n$$\ny=mx+b\n$$\n\nFirst, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\nm \\mid \\approx \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}}; = \\frac{7 - 4}{6 - 4}; = \\frac{3}{2}; = 1.5\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=1.5$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny = 1.5 x + b\n$$\n\nWe now need to estimate the $y$-intercept $b$. We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(4,4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= 1.5x + b \\\\\n4 &= 1.5(4) + b \\\\\n4 &= 6 + b \\\\\n- 2 &= b \\\\\nb &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is\n\n$$\ny = 1.5x - 2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152338 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "327d9a77-b2dd-57b1-b959-570684714bf9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Trendline of a Given Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98c199cc-b457-5100-a811-b770c11dec04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no linear trend in the data" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148963} {:answer/id #uuid "a0a21e45-42d1-5f04-b97d-424d712eb134" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148964} {:answer/id #uuid "29ce39ad-de7a-5ea5-b4fa-368cb0ca5dd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148965} {:answer/id #uuid "323d8b11-4d41-5c2f-b1b5-395f84634905" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148966} {:answer/id #uuid "735fa2fc-9d4a-5845-b0d1-332279944de6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "323d8b11-4d41-5c2f-b1b5-395f84634905" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148966} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5cddbed-708c-5216-ada4-a2e6b63a2ba6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148962}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fa90d9a6-e51c-5604-b79f-b37b09fca968" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-133633" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2609/Source/Images/q-133633.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between age and years of work experience among a particular group of workers. Which of the following could be the trend line for this scatter plot?" :question/worked-solution "The plot shows that the data points are scattered along a straight line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/c8597282ec934e535a01fa6f22be95b958d0393a5d0c5cd6358a9a7e620ba6a5.png)\n\nWe see that the line $q$ best fits the given data set."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247766 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "327d9a77-b2dd-57b1-b959-570684714bf9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Trendline of a Given Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08f3b38d-154c-5b12-9ffe-6be66ce0a9bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247768} {:answer/id #uuid "c2877d37-c07a-551b-a319-ca8b4b36ae30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no linear trend in the data" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247769} {:answer/id #uuid "c0865105-f19f-5352-822b-6049e0226937" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247770} {:answer/id #uuid "91d7f2b2-7a5b-5386-a9cf-ab95837d8992" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247771} {:answer/id #uuid "a8201eda-aced-538e-87c9-24418536900a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2877d37-c07a-551b-a319-ca8b4b36ae30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no linear trend in the data" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247769} :answer-field/id #uuid "0330203f-f0fc-50d7-938c-74c52b241237" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247767}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e76b127-8261-5bdd-91f7-28d466689876" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-133639" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/3e0b0fc97e260decaa74a9a751b6422714d1ca7365aff3cc05e57f8904b9067a.png)\n\nA company produces cars. The scatter plot above shows the correspondence between the number of cars produced each week and the company's profit, in thousands of dollars. Which of the following is the trend line of the scatter plot?" :question/worked-solution "The plot shows that the data points are scattered along a curve, not a straight line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/e960deb7d006d665abb97a83791204190af503f98dc3a23eae407e6c03e155df.png)\n\nTherefore, there is no linear trend in the data."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152341 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81fcd057-f612-59c5-9b08-3ba76a86c466" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148981} {:answer/id #uuid "a2e1e39c-5fa1-57bd-99db-e426f163b690" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148982} {:answer/id #uuid "e3255dbc-1dd7-5f10-89da-79b0da21ad78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148983} {:answer/id #uuid "12e9b896-4d0d-580c-8df4-bd7a0d38be75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148984} {:answer/id #uuid "51399fab-1112-53e4-80ce-46900a3154a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3255dbc-1dd7-5f10-89da-79b0da21ad78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148983} :answer-field/id #uuid "822e48ed-80d0-5479-9379-8225e9c2e4c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148980}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3eefe541-d677-50bc-bb17-f1cdd88a5e62" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-133765" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2609/Source/Images/q-133765.png)\n\nWhat is the slope of the trend line shown above." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(4,1)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(8,9).$\n\nTherefore, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-1}{8-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152342 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "890526df-fd1a-5340-8732-efc0c1a1b0ae" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abc2a489-ac1f-5be0-aed7-a8ec9ead57e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148987} {:answer/id #uuid "01d56ada-2acf-55e6-bd10-65939cf5ad4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148988} {:answer/id #uuid "05791f4c-57df-5dcf-b9d3-8f0f570b750d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148989} {:answer/id #uuid "2e8e0fa7-55d9-5a7d-89cf-93da30633896" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148990} {:answer/id #uuid "5759b492-5341-53fa-bcaa-d8d41aba7452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5759b492-5341-53fa-bcaa-d8d41aba7452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148991} :answer-field/id #uuid "58cb6b68-192b-5481-b429-1bc0b67793a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148986}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bf5281e3-0502-59b7-8231-a65966150dfe" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-133768" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2609/Source/Images/q-133768.png)\n\nEstimate the slope of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round your answer to the nearest $0.5$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/0575edf80f4a6f26c8f1002404ac04331d4c5d1f81b644021bc6284a6212338a.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(2,2)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(6,8).$\n\nTherefore, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-2}{6-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{4} \\\\  & =1.5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152343 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "890526df-fd1a-5340-8732-efc0c1a1b0ae" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc1bc6c4-e711-563b-b857-0289bb0d47af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-0.5x + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148993} {:answer/id #uuid "d1fa1b42-8978-5636-90eb-3677c4c9de41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-1.5x + 8.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148994} {:answer/id #uuid "d84817a4-2dd5-5f8a-b586-7695d1d031e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 1.5x - 8.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148995} {:answer/id #uuid "f5ec26d4-8aea-514f-950a-ce17bc25583e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 0.5x + 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148996} {:answer/id #uuid "fac803c9-708f-503b-9d7f-585758d709c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-0.5x + 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148997}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fac803c9-708f-503b-9d7f-585758d709c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-0.5x + 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148997} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ae6bf24-f591-5907-8565-9f82103ba09b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186148992}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be8af3f3-2d6e-5282-b124-c4fc21f05bfb" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-133769" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2609/Source/Images/q-133769.png)\n\nEstimate the equation of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round both the slope and the $y$-intercept to the nearest $0.5$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/fd3ce3de75fa9296c721e3f3a28bef241eae6350819c4cc7a54707921c0c1fe4.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(2,7)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(8,4).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-7}{8-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{6} \\\\  & =-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-0.5$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-0.5x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to estimate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,7):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-0.5x+b \\\\ 7 & =-0.5(2)+b \\\\ 7 & =-1+b \\\\ 8 & =b \\\\ b & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-0.5x+8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247773 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "327d9a77-b2dd-57b1-b959-570684714bf9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Trendline of a Given Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e23c4de8-edc1-5159-aa7f-11f7e7461977" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answ