ollowing is the trend line of the scatter plot?" :question/worked-solution "The plot shows that the data points are scattered along a curve, not a straight line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/00fe583ae8b83bfef31c1914489be7794aa4b7b2850cd01243a46b8d86d1dddb.png)\n\nTherefore, there is no linear trend in the data."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b36fd1f5-35cc-5130-89f6-70d53c09aee5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247796} {:answer/id #uuid "91dde2eb-3289-51bb-9c33-f6f018b32382" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247797} {:answer/id #uuid "4d66408e-62f4-5062-9348-7155371034f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247798} {:answer/id #uuid "1ce2c447-97b7-5668-af9a-b235a4eea186" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247799} {:answer/id #uuid "c11cafbc-eb70-5192-bbcf-20f8657e0ccb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b36fd1f5-35cc-5130-89f6-70d53c09aee5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247796} :answer-field/id #uuid "33b96466-10f7-5a39-98a1-d4a885f0cf31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247795}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9c657514-3c46-5f1c-8175-539557f1e6c3" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-134011" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/c55d326b26a8bb6831f38456b7b47878ef66a185090c7327cbb151c4e951be33.png)\n\nWhat is the slope of the trend line shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(3,2)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(5,1).$\n\nTherefore, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-2}{5-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247801 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b52e5e66-fe54-5898-ba03-5acce5527ef5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247803} {:answer/id #uuid "33abcfc9-59c6-5387-9d91-b39a3e79a16b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247804} {:answer/id #uuid "d97299a8-aa3c-52d4-9f77-de53c2a9e05d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247805} {:answer/id #uuid "62ff1108-b47a-5bd8-825f-b4d7c9f2fcd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247806} {:answer/id #uuid "0a46f265-1ccc-5848-a747-f5fe26d3c062" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b52e5e66-fe54-5898-ba03-5acce5527ef5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247803} :answer-field/id #uuid "5054ba7a-37e1-55ef-ba37-624f690540b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247802}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8fc30479-0ae1-5397-a71e-95530d9018e2" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-134013" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/72a4541fa9349de3a1d7218f3622ebb7536cc460bbf32fd90e43c754fac909a3.png)\n\nWhat is the slope of the trend line shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(0,-1)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(3,1).$\n\nTherefore, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-(-1)}{3-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247808 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dca10fd8-90c8-5c9f-991c-b72c852548ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{5}{7}x+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247810} {:answer/id #uuid "271c1441-92dd-5749-a225-2cc308cdca1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{6}{7}x+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247811} {:answer/id #uuid "ba58e62d-472c-5500-97ca-e724a8e2c73e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{2}{3}x+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247812} {:answer/id #uuid "dd475ef0-8f46-580c-9077-d17e7f8758b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{6}{7}x+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247813} {:answer/id #uuid "70379917-c5bd-5434-8cbc-f3d8ee725056" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{5}{7}x+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "271c1441-92dd-5749-a225-2cc308cdca1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{6}{7}x+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247811} :answer-field/id #uuid "baa20bd2-7fc3-54ff-a621-afe065059849" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247809}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0fd50200-c5bb-57f9-8883-bf1a29b8fe86" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-134019" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/31394106551498e7fd3a5cf57773f11ae31c7bc80c9a12272e95033bdcfd462e.png)\n\nDetermine the equation of the trend line shown above." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(0,9)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(7,3).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-9}{7-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6}{7} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-\\frac{6}{7}$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{6}{7}x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(0,9):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{6}{7}x+b \\\\ 9 & =-\\frac{6}{7}(0)+b \\\\ 9 & =0+b \\\\ b & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{6}{7}x+9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247815 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e78102d-ff88-586b-ba3a-50c68ff0b439" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{6}{5}x-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247817} {:answer/id #uuid "99ff009d-84f3-52e2-9e75-d2c333669fc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{7}{5}x-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247818} {:answer/id #uuid "5700f2a2-25ac-520b-b009-f748c7211115" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{8}{5}x-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247819} {:answer/id #uuid "138dc2ad-1379-5fa1-837a-4735ef7fc21f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{6}{5}x-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247820} {:answer/id #uuid "5d19758b-bd47-52c6-a3a4-0ac4db2868c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{7}{5}x-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "138dc2ad-1379-5fa1-837a-4735ef7fc21f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{6}{5}x-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247820} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c1abdaa-816d-5b68-a847-d70b8dee2562" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247816}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e2360671-96ab-5521-825d-76752c839c61" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-134023" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/1c9f30692222eaaed4cda6b608dcc1ccb01eefd6b5fa7730b5b8bb29c9f528b1.png)\n\nDetermine the equation of the trend line shown above." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(2,2)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(7,8).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-2}{7-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=\\frac{6}{5}$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{6}{5}x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{6}{5}x+b \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{6}{5}(2)+b \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{12}{5}+b \\\\ 10 & =12+5b \\\\ -2 & =5b \\\\ b & =-\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{6}{5}x-\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247822 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "890526df-fd1a-5340-8732-efc0c1a1b0ae" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96aa7826-18c7-5233-a1af-61234fa47138" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247824} {:answer/id #uuid "9b0beaf6-32cc-5017-a4e5-fba2ab01c6c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-1.5x+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247825} {:answer/id #uuid "28a165f6-3fa0-5290-ad54-1faf12b0de17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247826} {:answer/id #uuid "9c14989c-504d-54b8-82ae-adbda82b673f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-0.5x+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247827} {:answer/id #uuid "147cb5c3-b855-5a29-9c61-313f0722e002" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-0.5x+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96aa7826-18c7-5233-a1af-61234fa47138" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247824} :answer-field/id #uuid "7633dab5-aa8e-57f3-83d2-6313382bf24d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247823}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4ea3c63e-d2ec-56ec-acdc-942ec91b6a05" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-134031" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/111833881cf8e939d896f23a5ab7ca436f9265e7b8fd66c099eb118eab8fd6b0.png)\n\nEstimate the equation of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round both the slope and the $y$-intercept to the nearest $0.5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/fdad2c939372e14617ba4e393037d7f5852cd8114467aa914ccb8963c0eacfeb.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(2,5)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(6,1).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-5}{6-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{4} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-1$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to estimate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,5):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-x+b \\\\ 5 & =-2+b \\\\ 7 & =b \\\\ b & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-x+7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247829 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "890526df-fd1a-5340-8732-efc0c1a1b0ae" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c4da729-75ff-5299-af69-9e8ac36242a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247831} {:answer/id #uuid "df756c2b-c704-5ad5-9a24-ec07cdf51a7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2.5x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247832} {:answer/id #uuid "3092f54f-8f8e-5170-9c74-8f3e84b72cfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=1.5x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247833} {:answer/id #uuid "fa193485-8256-58f9-9c4b-55f4f697ef67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247834} {:answer/id #uuid "6bc4f3b7-26e4-5df3-b655-917928c75092" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=1.5x-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa193485-8256-58f9-9c4b-55f4f697ef67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247834} :answer-field/id #uuid "ede40fa3-2a42-5d3c-a69c-3f29eebcee88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247830}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7c5f022b-dc24-5d6e-9e31-83f3aaacf0d5" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-134032" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/d23d6a35343aebcb986118bd7c5bc720f00480706057ec900e55c75bac296ebb.png)\n\nEstimate the equation of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round both the slope and the $y$-intercept to the nearest $0.5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/663e4d77d51816641a9fa861f37893d9f986d5e2b00e605ed5eb4fc19d40eab4.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(5,5)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(7,9).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-5}{7-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=2$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=2x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to estimate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(5,5):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2x+b \\\\ 5 & =2(5)+b \\\\ 5 & =10+b \\\\ -5 & =b \\\\ b & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=2x-5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247836 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "890526df-fd1a-5340-8732-efc0c1a1b0ae" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec7b281b-c060-5115-ba7f-5f12a298bed9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3x+12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247838} {:answer/id #uuid "30bb6390-7c3b-5f68-b4c4-4d709f90c81a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-0.5x+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247839} {:answer/id #uuid "d7452534-b1e2-5615-9ed3-a9436967e6f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x+12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247840} {:answer/id #uuid "1b64ef8d-69a2-5d6b-b9de-a75b9f706368" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247841} {:answer/id #uuid "509f7578-fc59-56b3-803f-671282d51c22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2x+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "509f7578-fc59-56b3-803f-671282d51c22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2x+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247842} :answer-field/id #uuid "c24bdab6-a9a1-505c-8c97-8126c5747911" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247837}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5c3f41a-a5ad-5dad-b06b-1fd6da917e30" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-134033" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/24d3507598aa125a515534fd79c82e051875e897bedbe333cdaaf4e4856f67e4.png)\n\nEstimate the equation of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round both the slope and the $y$-intercept to the nearest $0.5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938989/assets/f62fe2cf8d93e0737482334a6f659202032160d451e6518afa152f43fb51d0a7.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(2,6)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(4,2).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-6}{4-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{2} \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-2$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-2x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to estimate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,6):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x+b \\\\ 6 & =-2(2)+b \\\\ 6 & =-4+b \\\\ 10 & =b \\\\ b & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-2x+10.\n$$"}]}
